  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased quality and labour market relevance of skills development and TVET</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO supports efforts to align vocational education and lifelong learning programs in Serbia with labour market needs. This involves strengthening the capacities of the Serbian Association of Employers, the Ministry of Education, and Sector Skills Councils in translating employers&#x2019; skill demands into actionable policies.  
In response to a request from the Serbian Association of Employers, the ILO conducted a Rapid Skills for Trade and Economic Diversification (STED) assessment in the hotel industry from June 2022 to September 2023, which was validated and launched in 2024. This initiative identified growth scenarios, skills needs, company capacity gaps, and priority actions for skills development. As a result, a Sector Skills Strategy for the hotel industry was developed with tripartite participation. 
To follow-up on some of the urgent needs identified in this strategy, the ILO will strengthen the capacities of Social Partners, the Ministries of Education, Labour and Tourism, as well as the Sector Skills Council for Tourism in the adaptation and development of skills training programmes to emerging skills needs in the tourism sector &#x2013; such as green and digital skills &#x2013; as well as in improving human resource development practices in companies.</narrative>
  </description>
